mbre se adjudicó el 10 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 8 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 64 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.985,12 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El límite de contratos no indica errores. Puede haber razones legítimas como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otras áreas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 88 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 13.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.7 to 9.2. December accounts for 10% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,985.12 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove misconduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate improper actions by the body or its contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to confirm the service type and whether it aligns with the body's needs. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service or if they cover distinct requirements. Look for patterns in December contracts to determine if they are part of a broader trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["h0Q0UhgKEZQS7pcxhTeWOg%3D%3D","uIlYP1AtIPz%2B3JAijK